      "id": "morrison",
      "title": "Grant Morrison",
      "sub": "Batman #655–683 and #700–702 · 2006–2010 · 26 issues",
      "intro": "Morrison spent seven years on Batman and used every comic ever published about him as raw material, on purpose — the fifties, the Silver Age, the bits everyone else quietly dropped. It is the most argued-about run here and the one that rewards knowing the history.\n\nThis is the main-title half of it. The run also carries on through Batman and Robin, The Return of Bruce Wayne and Batman Incorporated — three more books, and a rabbit hole this list does not carry. #659–662 and #670–671 sit between its chapters without being part of it; #670–671 are collected with The Resurrection of Ra's al Ghul instead.",
